To make Bootstrap tables sortable alphanumerically without using jQuery or other plugins, you can use the HTML5 Drag and Drop API. Here’s a step-by-step guide:

1. **HTML Structure**: Ensure your table has a structure that supports sorting. Each header cell (`<th>`) should have a unique identifier or class to distinguish it from other headers.

2. **CSS Styling**: Add some CSS to style the headers and indicate the sort direction. For example, you can add a class like `.sort-asc` or `.sort-desc` to show the current sort direction.

3. **JavaScript Implementation**: Use the HTML5 Drag and Drop API to handle the sorting logic. Here’s a basic example:

```html
<table class="table">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th draggable="true" id="col1">Name</th>
      <th draggable="true" id="col2">Age</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Alice</td>
      <td>25</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Bob</td>
      <td>30</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<script>
  const headers = document.querySelectorAll('th[draggable="true"]');
  const rows = document.querySelectorAll('tbody tr');

  headers.forEach(header => {
    header.addEventListener('dragstart', (e) => {
      e.dataTransfer.setData('text/plain', header.id);
    });
  });

  rows.forEach(row => {
    row.addEventListener('dragover', (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
    });

    row.addEventListener('drop', (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      const draggedHeaderId = e.dataTransfer.getData('text/plain');
      const draggedHeader = document.getElementById(draggedHeaderId);
      const currentSortDirection = draggedHeader.classList.contains('sort-asc') ? 'desc' : 'asc';
      draggedHeader.classList.remove('sort-asc', 'sort-desc');
      draggedHeader.classList.add(`sort-${currentSortDirection}`);

      // Sort the rows based on the header
      const columnData = Array.from(rows).map(row => row.cells[Array.from(headers).findIndex(h => h.id === draggedHeaderId)].textContent);
      const sortedRows = columnData.sort((a, b) => {
        if (currentSortDirection === 'asc') {
          return a.localeCompare(b);
        } else {
          return b.localeCompare(a);
        }
      });

      rows.forEach((row, index) => {
        row.remove();
        document.querySelector('tbody').appendChild(row);
      });

      // Reorder the rows based on the sorted data
      sortedRows.forEach((data, index) => {
        const row = rows[index];
        row.cells[Array.from(headers).findIndex(h => h.id === draggedHeaderId)].textContent = data;
      });
    });
  });
</script>
```

This code sets up the table to be sortable by dragging and dropping the headers. When a header is dragged, it stores the header ID. When a row is dropped, it sorts the rows based on the column under the dragged header and updates the sort direction.

What is the purpose of the `draggable` attribute in the table headers?

The `draggable` attribute in the table headers allows the user to drag the headers to sort the table. When set to `true`, it enables the header to be dragged, and the browser will trigger the drag and drop events, which can be handled by JavaScript to perform the sorting logic.

